    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. so you're saying the decison is basically ours to make? but wouldn't you say that the momentum of capital and the competitive pressure between nations makes a \"controlled\" transition almost impossible in practice? it feels like even if one country tries to regulate it, the rest of the world just pushes ahead to not get left behind. is it really a choice if the alternative is total economic irrelevance?",
